  "solution": [
    "Rectangle \\(ABCE\\): \\(16 \\times 6 = 96\\).",
    "Triangle \\(CDE\\) is isosceles with base \\(CE = 16\\), so the altitude from \\(D\\) meets \\(\\overline{CE}\\) at its midpoint, 8 from each end. Its height is \\(\\sqrt{10^{2} - 8^{2}} = 6\\).",
    "Triangle area: \\(\\frac{1}{2}(16)(6) = 48\\). Pentagon: \\(96 + 48 = 144\\)."
  ],
  "explanation": null,
  "traps": null,
  "verify": "P=figure['points']\nCE=P['C'][0]-P['E'][0]\nassert CE==16 and P['C'][1]-P['B'][1]==6\nh=sqrt(10**2-(CE/2)**2)\nassert h==P['D'][1]-P['C'][1]==6\nans=CE*6+Rational(1,2)*CE*h\nassert ans==144\nassert Rational(spr_answers[0])==ans\n",
